---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Quote from '../components/Quote.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

import heroImage from '../assets/photos/monthly-narayana-seva-hall-01.jpg';
import mataImage from '../assets/mata-vishwatmananda-giri.jpg';
import kitchenImage from '../assets/photos/kitchen-preparation-01.jpg';
import serviceImage from '../assets/photos/narayana-seva-village-01.jpg';

const pillars = [
  {
    label: 'Who we are',
    text: 'A public charitable trust and spiritual centre in Puttaparthi, offering a platform to spiritual aspirants of every faith. A community of volunteers, not a staff — nobody here is employed to be compassionate.',
  },
  {
    label: 'What we do',
    text: 'Daily worship, and daily service: meals cooked and carried, free medical camps, free tuition, drinking water without charge, and food for the animals around us.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Why we serve',
    text: 'Because we were told plainly that every action performed with devotion is itself a spiritual practice. Service is not a good deed added to worship. It is the worship.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Whom we serve',
    text: 'Anyone in need, without reference to caste, creed or faith — elders living alone, patients who cannot afford care, children whose schooling needs help, families short of water.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Sri Sathya Sai Kuteer is a public charitable trust and spiritual centre in Puttaparthi, established in 2017 under the guidance of Bhagavan Sri Sathya Sai Baba through Mata Vishwatmananda Giri."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About the Kuteer"
    title="A house built to be given away"
    lede="Sri Sathya Sai Kuteer was raised on a single instruction: that a place of practice should be inseparable from a place of service."
    image={heroImage}
    imageAlt="Guests seated together for lunch in the Kuteer hall during the monthly Narayana Seva"
  />

  {/* ------------------------------------------------------------ Pillars */}
  <Section space="md">
    <div class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-ink-900/10 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        pillars.map((p) => (
          <div class="reveal bg-paper p-8 sm:p-10">
            <p class="eyebrow">{p.label}</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-700">{p.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* -------------------------------------------------------------- Story */}
  <Section tone="deep" space="lg">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.15fr] lg:gap-20">
      <div class="reveal order-2 lg:order-1">
        <figure>
          <Image
            src={mataImage}
            alt="Swamini Mata Vishwatmananda Giri"
            widths={[420, 720]}
            sizes="(min-width:1024px) 22rem, 80vw"
            class="arch-soft aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover object-top"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption class="mt-5 border-l-2 border-gold-300 pl-4">
            <p class="font-display text-[1.15rem] font-semibold text-ink-900">Swamini Mata Vishwatmananda Giri</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
              Gurumata of the Kuteer. It was to her that the instruction to build this place was given, and it is under
              her guidance that everything here is carried out.
            </p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:gap-5">
          <Image
            src={kitchenImage}
            alt="Volunteers preparing vegetables in the Kuteer kitchen"
            widths={[300, 600]}
            sizes="(min-width:1024px) 11rem, 45vw"
            class="aspect-square w-full rounded-xl object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <Image
            src={serviceImage}
            alt="A volunteer visiting an elderly resident in a village near Puttaparthi"
            widths={[300, 600]}
            sizes="(min-width:1024px) 11rem, 45vw"
            class="aspect-square w-full rounded-xl object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="order-1 lg:order-2">
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="How it began" title="January 2017, and an instruction" />
        <div class="prose-kuteer mt-7">
          <p>
            In January 2017, Bhagavan Sri Sathya Sai Baba instructed <strong>Mata Vishwatmananda Giri</strong> — through
            direct conversation — to construct <em>Sri Sathya Sai Kuteer</em>. He said this place would become a centre
            of <em>sadhana</em> for thousands of seekers, and that <strong
              >Lord Panchamukhi Anjaneya Swamy is its Kshetrapalaka</strong
            >, the guardian deity of the site.
          </p>
          <p>
            Through Jnani Bele, Bhagavan Baba then made the practical path possible: the mobilising of funds, the
            acquisition of the land, the <em>Bhoomi Puja</em>, the architectural style of the buildings, even the choice
            of builder. The Kuteer was inaugurated on <strong>24 December 2017</strong>, on Christmas Day.
          </p>
          <p>
            What that instruction produced is not a monument. It is a kitchen that starts before dawn, a water plant that
            never switches off, a hall that becomes a clinic on the 23rd of the month and a classroom every evening.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-9">
          <Button href="/anjaneya-command/" variant="outline">Read Anjaneya's command</Button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ------------------------------------------------------------- Quote */}
  <section class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-ink-950 py-24 sm:py-28">
    <div
      class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-24 left-1/2 h-[26rem] w-[42rem] -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-[radial-gradient(circle,rgba(192,141,51,0.18),transparent_70%)]"
    >
    </div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 sm:px-8">
      <Quote cite="The guardian deity's message">
        In a sense, this is not merely an <em class="not-italic">Ashram</em> — a hermitage — but a true <em
          class="not-italic">Aashrayam</em
        >: a sanctuary, a refuge.
      </Quote>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* -------------------------------------------------------- Guidance */}
  <Section space="lg">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
      <div>
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="Guidance" title="Under whose grace this runs" />
        <div class="prose-kuteer mt-7">
          <p>
            Every activity at the Kuteer is carried out with the grace and blessings of <strong
              >Gurumata Mata Vishwatmanandagiri</strong
            >, <strong>Sadguru Sri Anjaneya Swamy</strong> and <strong>Bhagavan Sri Sathya Sai Baba</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Their teaching sets the terms of the work: that any action performed with devotion — while respecting all
            faiths and transcending caste and religion — is a spiritual practice which fosters wisdom and lifts the
            individual soul. That is why the Kuteer draws no line between what happens at the <em>homa kunda</em> and what
            happens at the cooking vessel.
          </p>
          <p>
            That teaching has been set down in writing and given as talks. Both are offered free: thirteen <a
              href="/books/">volumes to download</a
            >, and a growing archive of <a href="/media/">recorded satsangs and talks</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <SectionHeading eyebrow="How we work" title="Principles we hold to" />
        <div class="prose-kuteer mt-7">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Nothing is charged.</strong> No meal, no consultation, no medicine, no litre of water, no tuition hour.</li>
            <li><strong>No one is asked their caste or their creed.</strong> Need is the only qualification.</li>
            <li><strong>The recipient is not below the giver.</strong> We call those we serve <em>Narayanas</em> — the Divine, come to receive.</li>
            <li><strong>Regularity over spectacle.</strong> Daily and monthly, unbroken since 2017, is worth more than an occasional grand gesture.</li>
            <li><strong>Volunteers, not staff.</strong> The cooking, packing, delivering and teaching is done by members of this community.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <CallToAction
    eyebrow="Come and see"
    title="You are welcome at the Kuteer."
    text="Visitors may join the Geetha Homam at 9:00 AM on any day, and the monthly Narayana Seva on the 23rd. No appointment, no introduction needed."
    primary={{ href: '/contact/', label: 'Plan a visit' }}
    secondary={{ href: '/seva/', label: 'Our activities' }}
  />
</BaseLayout>
